## *Caparo Industries plc v Dickman* — three-stage duty-of-care test
##
## Source: *Caparo Industries plc v Dickman* [1990] UKHL 2, [1990] 2 AC
## 605. The House of Lords laid down the modern English test for the
## existence of a duty of care: a duty arises only where all three
## stages are made out conjunctively:
##
##   (a) Foreseeability — harm to the claimant was reasonably
##       foreseeable.
##   (b) Proximity — there was a relationship of sufficient proximity
##       (or "neighbourhood") between the parties.
##   (c) Fair, just and reasonable — it is fair, just and reasonable in
##       all the circumstances to impose a duty.
##
## The third limb is the policy gate: even if foreseeability and
## proximity are made out, the court may decline to impose a duty
## where doing so would be incoherent or open the floodgates.
##
## ADGM CFI applies *Caparo* directly via the *Application of English
## Law Regulations 2015* in every negligent-misstatement and
## professional-negligence claim. *Hedley Byrne v Heller* (a separate
## module) supplies the special-relationship rule for liability for
## words rather than acts.
##
## Used implicitly across:
##   - ADGM negligent-misstatement / professional-negligence cases
##     in the gold set (auditor liability, financial advice, etc.).

```catala
declaration structure CaparoFacts:
  data harm_reasonably_foreseeable content boolean
  data sufficient_proximity content boolean
  data fair_just_reasonable_to_impose content boolean

declaration structure DutyOfCareDisposition:
  data n_stages_satisfied content integer
  data duty_of_care_owed content boolean

declaration scope CaparoTest:
  input facts content CaparoFacts
  output disposition content DutyOfCareDisposition

scope CaparoTest:
  definition disposition equals
    let foreseeable equals facts.harm_reasonably_foreseeable in
    let proximity equals facts.sufficient_proximity in
    let fjr equals facts.fair_just_reasonable_to_impose in
    let satisfied equals
      (if foreseeable then 1 else 0)
      + (if proximity then 1 else 0)
      + (if fjr then 1 else 0)
    in
    DutyOfCareDisposition {
      -- n_stages_satisfied: satisfied
      -- duty_of_care_owed: foreseeable and proximity and fjr
    }
```

## Tests — all three stages and the policy-gate fallthrough.

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestCaparoAllStagesMet:
  composite scope CaparoTest
  output disposition content DutyOfCareDisposition

scope TestCaparoAllStagesMet:
  definition disposition equals composite.disposition
  definition composite.facts equals
    CaparoFacts {
      -- harm_reasonably_foreseeable: true
      -- sufficient_proximity: true
      -- fair_just_reasonable_to_impose: true
    }
  assertion disposition.duty_of_care_owed = true
  assertion disposition.n_stages_satisfied = 3

#[test] declaration scope TestCaparoFailsOnPolicyGate:
  composite scope CaparoTest
  output disposition content DutyOfCareDisposition

scope TestCaparoFailsOnPolicyGate:
  definition disposition equals composite.disposition
  ## Foreseeability + proximity made out, but the policy gate (fair,
  ## just, reasonable) cuts the duty — Caparo itself was decided this
  ## way against the auditor.
  definition composite.facts equals
    CaparoFacts {
      -- harm_reasonably_foreseeable: true
      -- sufficient_proximity: true
      -- fair_just_reasonable_to_impose: false
    }
  assertion disposition.duty_of_care_owed = false
  assertion disposition.n_stages_satisfied = 2
```
